From root@garbled.net  Sun Feb 7 08:47:07 1999
From: Tim Rightnour <root@garbled.net>
To: ds55@dimensional.com
Date: Sun, 07 Feb 1999 08:47:07 +0000
Subject: RE: Fw: Now what?

On 06-Feb-99 David Sullivan spoke unto us all:
# >Using the new two-part floppy, I was able to install (successfully) NetBSD
# >onto an IDE laptop drive inside my Multia/UDB.  But how do I boot it given
# >that:
# >
# >(1) No IDE devices are accessible from the SRM prompt;

One cannot boot off an IDE device on a multia.  The SRM is not capable of doing
so.  (SRM limitation, not NetBSD's)  I have however booted off floppy, and used
incantations of chroot to get my machine up multiuser in similar
circumstances..  Your best bet however would be a small scsi drive you could
stuff root onto.

