From cjs@cynic.net  Fri Feb 12 09:58:27 1999
From: Curt Sampson <cjs@cynic.net>
To: deker@digitaladdiction.com
Date: Fri, 12 Feb 1999 09:58:27 +0000
Subject: Re: 1.3.3 boot problem

On Fri, 12 Feb 1999, Rob Deker wrote:

>   I've got 2 UDB/Multias running 1.3.3 and I've got a little problem. I 
> can't seem to get them to autoboot into multi-user mode. I've made sure
> that $rc_configured is set to YES, but they always come up in single
> user mode. What am I missing?

For compatability with Digital Unix, you have to specify the `a'
option when you boot, otherwise it boots single-user. At the console
prompt, type `set boot_osflags a'.

This is for compatability with Digital Unix (or whatever Digital/Compaq
is calling it today). Why we want to be compatable in this way I'm
not sure, though....

cjs
